`storage gen` (#393) plans the router's storages from the registry and a small
deployment file — the RFC 09 §2 block, with the two things a human types wrong
derived instead: `strip_prefix` as the literal leftmost run of the selector,
and `garbage_collection.lifespan` as ceil(max covered `ttl_s` × margin), with
the computation shown (§2.3). The fixture registry's longest state `ttl_s` is
the catalog's one-year alias; the fleet's own alerts are 900 s, so the two
storages get different lifespans from the same rule.

Offline here, like every other registry-aware case: the dead-bus fixture
fails at once and the `--registry` dirs answer alone.

```console
$ zenctl storage gen --deployment tests/cmd/fixtures/storages.toml --registry ../fixture-tests/registry --zenoh-config tests/cmd/fixtures/dead-bus.json5 --format table
no session (failed to open the Zenoh session); answering from --registry only: ../fixture-tests/registry.
That is what this checkout declares, not what the fleet serves — `zenctl doctor --registry <dir>` compares them when the bus is reachable (RFC 05 §3.1).
storage plan for base "zensight"  (registry: 11 slice(s), longest state ttl_s 31536000 (catalog/alias/{old_id}))

volumes:
  fs        fs        durable · latest
  influxdb  influxdb  durable · all     url="http://localhost:8086"

storages:
  catalog       zensight/v1/@catalog/state/**       fs (latest)
    strip zensight/v1/@catalog/state  ·  covers 8 declared subject(s)
    gc lifespan 63072000 s (period 30 s): max ttl_s 31536000 (catalog/alias/{old_id}) × 2.0 = 63072000 s
    ! overlap: overlaps pdns_history (zensight/v1/@catalog/state/pdns/**): a GET under both selectors is answered by both, duplicate and possibly divergent — accept it (subscribers are unaffected; GET consumers consolidate) or carve one selector out of the other (RFC 09 §2)
  latest        zensight/v1/*/state/**              fs (latest)     replicated, complete
    strip zensight/v1  ·  covers 61 declared subject(s)
    gc lifespan 1800 s (period 30 s): max ttl_s 900 (gnmi/artifact/{kind}) × 2.0 = 1800 s
  pdns_history  zensight/v1/@catalog/state/pdns/**  influxdb (all)
    strip zensight/v1/@catalog/state/pdns  ·  covers 1 declared subject(s)
    gc lifespan 172800 s (period 30 s): max ttl_s 86400 (catalog/pdns/{ip_slug}) × 2.0 = 172800 s
    ! retention_is_the_databases: retention is the database's policy (an InfluxDB retention policy), not zenoh config: garbage_collection prunes metadata and never drops a value, so this storage's data grows until the database prunes it — size the volume against the write rate (RFC 09 §2.3)
    ! overlap: overlaps catalog (zensight/v1/@catalog/state/**): a GET under both selectors is answered by both, duplicate and possibly divergent — accept it (subscribers are unaffected; GET consumers consolidate) or carve one selector out of the other (RFC 09 §2)
  timeseries    zensight/v1/*/telemetry/**          influxdb (all)
    strip zensight/v1  ·  covers 356 declared subject(s)
    gc lifespan 86400 s (period 30 s): no state subject under this selector: RFC 09 §2.3 default 86400 s
    ! retention_is_the_databases: retention is the database's policy (an InfluxDB retention policy), not zenoh config: garbage_collection prunes metadata and never drops a value, so this storage's data grows until the database prunes it — size the volume against the write rate (RFC 09 §2.3)
4 storage(s) on 2 volume(s) planned, 0 refused
`--json5` emits the zenohd plugins.storage_manager block; `--check` compares it with what a router runs; `--explain <key>` says which storage takes a key

```

`--json5` is the file: the `plugins.storage_manager` block `zenohd` reads, with
every derivation and warning as a comment beside the storage it concerns. A
foreign schema, so it is a flag of its own and not a `--format` (#243).

```console
$ zenctl storage gen --deployment tests/cmd/fixtures/storages.toml --registry ../fixture-tests/registry --zenoh-config tests/cmd/fixtures/dead-bus.json5 --json5
no session (failed to open the Zenoh session); answering from --registry only: ../fixture-tests/registry.
That is what this checkout declares, not what the fleet serves — `zenctl doctor --registry <dir>` compares them when the bus is reachable (RFC 05 §3.1).
// zenohd storage_manager block — generated by `zenctl storage gen` (RFC 09 §2).
// base "zensight"; registry: 11 slice(s), longest state ttl_s 31536000 (catalog/alias/{old_id}).
// Merge under the router config's `plugins`; every non-memory volume needs its backend plugin installed, version-matched to the router.
plugins: {
  storage_manager: {
    volumes: {
      fs: {},  // durable · latest (RFC 09 §2.1)
      influxdb: { url: "http://localhost:8086" },  // durable · all (RFC 09 §2.1)
    },
    storages: {
      // catalog: class catalog; 8 declared subject(s) under it
      // ! overlap: overlaps pdns_history (zensight/v1/@catalog/state/pdns/**): a GET under both selectors is answered by both, duplicate and possibly divergent — accept it (subscribers are unaffected; GET consumers consolidate) or carve one selector out of the other (RFC 09 §2)
      catalog: {
        key_expr: "zensight/v1/@catalog/state/**",
        strip_prefix: "zensight/v1/@catalog/state",  // derived: the literal leftmost run of key_expr
        volume: { id: "fs", dir: "catalog" },
        garbage_collection: { period: 30, lifespan: 63072000 },  // max ttl_s 31536000 (catalog/alias/{old_id}) × 2.0 = 63072000 s (RFC 09 §2.3)
      },
      // latest: class state; 61 declared subject(s) under it
      latest: {
        key_expr: "zensight/v1/*/state/**",
        strip_prefix: "zensight/v1",  // derived: the literal leftmost run of key_expr
        volume: { id: "fs", dir: "latest" },
        replication: { hot: 6, interval: 10.0, propagation_delay: 250, sub_intervals: 5, warm: 30 },  // identical on every replica (RFC 09 §2.2)
        complete: true,  // replicated, fully covering latest storage (RFC 09 §2.2)
        garbage_collection: { period: 30, lifespan: 1800 },  // max ttl_s 900 (gnmi/artifact/{kind}) × 2.0 = 1800 s (RFC 09 §2.3)
      },
      // pdns_history: class catalog-pdns; 1 declared subject(s) under it
      // ! retention_is_the_databases: retention is the database's policy (an InfluxDB retention policy), not zenoh config: garbage_collection prunes metadata and never drops a value, so this storage's data grows until the database prunes it — size the volume against the write rate (RFC 09 §2.3)
      // ! overlap: overlaps catalog (zensight/v1/@catalog/state/**): a GET under both selectors is answered by both, duplicate and possibly divergent — accept it (subscribers are unaffected; GET consumers consolidate) or carve one selector out of the other (RFC 09 §2)
      pdns_history: {
        key_expr: "zensight/v1/@catalog/state/pdns/**",
        strip_prefix: "zensight/v1/@catalog/state/pdns",  // derived: the literal leftmost run of key_expr
        volume: { id: "influxdb", db: "pdns" },
        garbage_collection: { period: 30, lifespan: 172800 },  // max ttl_s 86400 (catalog/pdns/{ip_slug}) × 2.0 = 172800 s (RFC 09 §2.3)
      },
      // timeseries: class telemetry; 356 declared subject(s) under it
      // ! retention_is_the_databases: retention is the database's policy (an InfluxDB retention policy), not zenoh config: garbage_collection prunes metadata and never drops a value, so this storage's data grows until the database prunes it — size the volume against the write rate (RFC 09 §2.3)
      timeseries: {
        key_expr: "zensight/v1/*/telemetry/**",
        strip_prefix: "zensight/v1",  // derived: the literal leftmost run of key_expr
        volume: { id: "influxdb", db: "telemetry" },
        garbage_collection: { period: 30, lifespan: 86400 },  // no state subject under this selector: RFC 09 §2.3 default 86400 s (RFC 09 §2.3)
      },
    },
  },
}
