```

```console
$ zenctl storage gen --deployment tests/cmd/fixtures/storages.toml --json5 --format json
? 2
error: the argument '--json5' cannot be used with '--format <FORMAT>'

--json5 emits a foreign document format — somebody else's schema — while --format chooses among zenctl's own three renderings of a report. Drop one.

Usage: zenctl <COMMAND>

For more information, try '--help'.

```

`--explain <key>` is pure over the plan: which storage takes the key, and
why — and, for a service's state, why `latest` does not (`*` never matches an
`@`-chunk, RFC 03 §4 D4).

```console
$ zenctl storage gen --deployment tests/cmd/fixtures/storages.toml --registry ../fixture-tests/registry --zenoh-config tests/cmd/fixtures/dead-bus.json5 --format table --explain 'zensight/v1/@catalog/state/entity/x'
no session (failed to open the Zenoh session); answering from --registry only: ../fixture-tests/registry.
That is what this checkout declares, not what the fleet serves — `zenctl doctor --registry <dir>` compares them when the bus is reachable (RFC 05 §3.1).
zensight/v1/@catalog/state/entity/x
  → catalog  zensight/v1/@catalog/state/**  includes it
      class catalog under base "zensight": zensight/v1/@catalog/state/** includes every key zensight/v1/@catalog/state/entity/x names; stored under strip_prefix "zensight/v1/@catalog/state" on volume fs (latest)

```

A refusal names the storage and leaves the rest of the plan standing. Three
here, each for its own reason: replication on an all-mode volume is what the
storage manager refuses at startup (§2.2), so the plan refuses first; a volume
nobody declared; a class the registry declares nothing under — empty coverage
is a finding, not a plan. With nothing left to emit, `gen` exits 2: the input
was refused whole, and an act with nothing to do has no 1 to give.

```console
$ zenctl storage gen --deployment tests/cmd/fixtures/storages-refused.toml --registry ../fixture-tests/registry --zenoh-config tests/cmd/fixtures/dead-bus.json5 --format ndjson
? 2
no session (failed to open the Zenoh session); answering from --registry only: ../fixture-tests/registry.
That is what this checkout declares, not what the fleet serves — `zenctl doctor --registry <dir>` compares them when the bus is reachable (RFC 05 §3.1).
