`--check` is a verdict verb: a session that will not open lands on the
reserved 2, never on the 1 that would claim a difference this run never
measured (`zenctl/src/exit.rs`).

```console
$ zenctl storage gen --deployment tests/cmd/fixtures/storages.toml --check --zenoh-config tests/cmd/fixtures/dead-bus.json5
? 2
Error: failed to open the Zenoh session

Caused by:
    Unable to connect to any of [Single(tcp/127.0.0.1:1)]!
storage gen --check: the question could not be asked — exit 2, the reserved non-verdict (1 here would claim a verdict this run never reached)

```

A deployment file this tool cannot read is its input refused — exit 2, with
serde's own wording naming the key it did not know.

```console
$ zenctl storage gen --deployment tests/cmd/fixtures/no-such-deployment.toml
? 2
Error: --deployment: cannot read tests/cmd/fixtures/no-such-deployment.toml: No such file or directory (os error 2)

```
